{
  "schema": "elder-souls/npcs@1",
  "group": "mainline",
  "owner": "W1-19 — the main quest, end to end",
  "source": "The people the mainline names. Every `giver.npc_id`, every `deceit.revealed_by[].source` that is a person, and every id that appears as a key of `consequences.npc_disposition` in game/data/quests/mainline-act1..5.json and mainline-backpath.json. Written because the quests referred to twenty-six people who did not exist as records anywhere in the build, which made `giver.disposition_min` unreachable and made the mainline unofferable from a cold start.",
  "consumed_by": "game/src/engine.js seedDispositions() — `disposition` here is copied into sim.quest.dispositions at boot and on every reset, which is what QuestEngine.context() reads and what gate.js canOffer() checks against giver.disposition_min. Before W1-19 nothing in the build read this field on any NPC record in any file, so every authored disposition in game/data/npcs/** was inert and every quest with a disposition_min was unofferable without a Charm spell.",
  "declared_incomplete": true,
  "declared_incomplete_note": "Wave 1. These records carry id, name, race, settlement, disposition, topics and one greeting line each. Schedules, services and interiors are W1-04's and W1-17's and are not filled here. reaction_group and actor were filled by W1-07 round 4: without a reaction_group the quest-offer gate reads the same disposition for every race, which is exactly the defect that round was dispatched to close, and Engine._assertGiversAreVisibleToRace() now refuses to boot without them.",
